{
  "result": "If I could change just one thing, I'd make it so no one ever has to worry about basic survival.\n\nNot making everyone rich, or making everyone the same \u2014 just a solid floor that no one can fall below. Enough food, clean water, a safe place to sleep, basic healthcare, and a decent education for every kid.\n\nI pick that one because so much else flows from it.\n\nIt's hard to learn, create, take risks, care for your family, or think long-term about things like the climate when you're focused on getting through today. A lot of fear, disease, conflict, and desperation doesn't come from people being bad \u2014 it comes from people feeling trapped and insecure.\n\nIf that baseline fear were gone, billions of people would suddenly get their time and imagination back. More kids would stay in school. More good ideas would actually get tried. People would be freer to leave bad situations, help their neighbors, disagree without it feeling existential, and build a life based on what they care about, not just what they need to survive.\n\nIt wouldn't fix everything, and I don't think it should. People would still grieve, get heartbroken, argue, fail, and have to figure out what a meaningful life looks like. That struggle is part of being human. I'd just want to remove the *needless* suffering that stops people from getting a fair chance at it.\n\nWhat would your one change be?",
